      "title": "Hypothetical Checklist for Offline Local LLM Testing (Generation & Network)",
      "body": "This post outlines a hypothetical checklist for testing local LLMs offline, based on a synthetic experimental brief. The core idea is to verify a model's functionality without an internet connection. The proposed steps focus on two key areas: ensuring the model can still generate text and confirming it makes no unintended network requests. Fact F1 states that models can be downloaded beforehand, which is a prerequisite for any offline testing. Fact F2 specifies that the offline verification must encompass both text generation and monitoring for network activity. It's crucial to remember, as per Fact F3, that no actual offline test has been performed in this scenario; this is purely a planning exercise. The objective is to establish a structured approach for future hypothetical evaluations. We aim to confirm that a downloaded model operates entirely locally as expected. Further discussion on refining these hypothetical steps would be welcome.",
