      "title": "Planning a Hypothetical Offline Test for Local LLMs: Generation & Network Monitoring",
      "body": "This is a guide for a hypothetical experiment to test local LLMs in an offline environment. The scenario, based on synthetic input, allows for pre-downloading models (F1). The primary goal is to validate that a model operates entirely without network access after disconnection. The proposed test procedure involves two main components: first, verifying the model's ability to generate coherent text, and second, actively monitoring for any network requests initiated by the model or its associated processes. This rigorous check ensures true offline operation. Importantly, this entire process is a hypothetical exercise as detailed in Fact F3; no actual offline tests have been conducted. The intention is to create a robust framework for evaluating offline LLM capabilities. We are interested in feedback on the completeness of this hypothetical testing plan, particularly regarding the generation and network monitoring aspects.",
